# Markdown TOC Generation

When generating or updating a table of contents (TOC) in a markdown file:

## Does not apply to Cursor agent assets

Do **not** add or refresh content-doc TOC blocks on:

- `cursor-config/skills/**` (`SKILL.md` and supporting skill markdown)
- `cursor-config/rules/**` (`.mdc` rules)

Cursor skills use YAML frontmatter at the top of `SKILL.md` per the Cursor skill convention — not `#` title + `## Table of contents`.

## TOC rules (content documentation)

- Do NOT include the document title (h1 heading) in the TOC entries.
- Do NOT include a self-referencing "Table of contents" entry.
- Do NOT include `## Project structure` in the TOC (auto-generated block).
- Start the TOC at the first h2 section below the title.

Use `cursor-config/scripts/update_markdown_docs.py --toc-only` or the `markdown-toc` skill. Wrap generated TOC entries in `<!-- markdown-toc:start -->` / `<!-- markdown-toc:end -->` markers.

Example — given this document structure:

```markdown
# My Document Title

## Table of contents
<!-- markdown-toc:start -->
...
<!-- markdown-toc:end -->

## First Section
### Subsection A
## Second Section
```

The TOC should be:

```markdown
<!-- markdown-toc:start -->
- [First Section](#first-section)
  - [Subsection A](#subsection-a)
- [Second Section](#second-section)
<!-- markdown-toc:end -->
```
